{"type": "root", "attrs": {"index": "no"}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Generate mattes based on image colors (keying)"], "extent": [12, 63]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Houdini includes several operators to let you isolate, select, and/or\nremove areas of color."], "extent": [107, 201]}, {"tag": "table", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 0, "extent": [201, 209], "body": [{"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [209, 218], "body": [{"tag": "th", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" To do this\u2026"], "extent": [218, 245]}, {"tag": "th", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Use this operator"], "extent": [245, 276]}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [276, 285], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Remove color and produce alpha mattes."], "extent": [285, 337]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [337, 350], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/chromakey", "type": "link", "text": ["Chromakey"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/chromakey.html"}], "extent": [350, 394]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [394, 403], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Copy the luminance to the alpha channel."], "extent": [403, 457]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [457, 470], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/lumamatte", "type": "link", "text": ["Luma Matte"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/lumamatte.html"}], "extent": [470, 515]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [515, 524], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Replace one color with another."], "extent": [524, 569]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [569, 582], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/colorreplace", "type": "link", "text": ["Color Replace"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/colorreplace.html"}], "extent": [582, 633]}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"tag": "tr", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 4, "extent": [633, 642], "body": [{"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "text": [" Mask luminance in/outside a certain range."], "extent": [642, 698]}, {"tag": "td", "attrs": {}, "type": "pxml", "indent": 8, "extent": [698, 711], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 12, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/lumakey", "type": "link", "text": ["Lumakey"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/lumakey.html"}], "extent": [711, 752]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true}, {"type": "tip_group", "body": [{"type": "tip", "indent": 0, "role": "item", "extent": [752, 757], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/chromakey", "type": "link", "text": ["Chromakey"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/chromakey.html"}, ", ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/colorreplace", "type": "link", "text": ["Color Replace"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/colorreplace.html"}, ", and ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/lumamatte", "type": "link", "text": ["Lumakey"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/lumamatte.html"}, "\n    operators have a ", {"type": "em", "text": ["supersample"]}, " parameter, which gives anti-aliased\n    edges at sharp color transitions. A supersample value of 3 is\n    usually sufficient. Higher values will really slow down the\n    operation. If you don\u2019t want antialiased edges, set supersampling to\n    1."], "extent": [757, 1154]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["To select areas of color interactively (like the Magic Wand in\nPhotoshop), make the node active (select the node in the network editor\nand press ", {"keys": ["Enter"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, " in the viewer) and use the following keys:"], "extent": [1154, 1353]}, {"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["Press ", {"keys": ["O"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, ", then brush-select over pixels of the colors you want to\n  isolate, or hold ", {"keys": ["Ctrl"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, " and drag out a selection box. Click ", {"keys": ["RMB"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, "\n  to finish the selection."], "extent": [1353, 1524]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["To select the drop-off region interactively, press ", {"keys": ["L"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, " instead of\n  ", {"keys": ["O"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, " to begin selecting."], "extent": [1524, 1623]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["To add to the current selection instead of replacing it, press ", {"keys": ["Shift\n", "O"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, " or ", {"keys": ["Shift", "L"], "type": "keys", "text": null}, "."], "extent": [1623, 1723]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": ["If you don\u2019t want the selection to affect Alpha (normally it creates\n  an alpha matte from the keying operation), unscope the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["A"]}, " plane on\n  the operator\u2019s ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Mask"]}, " tab (and remove the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["*"]}, " if you have deep\n  raster planes you don\u2019t want affected)."], "extent": [1723, 1975]}], "container": true}], "title": ["Generate mattes based on image colors (keying)"], "included": ["/composite/_old_cops_deprecated"]}